    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Wakefield/Teaching-Fellow---Foundation-Science_R31504": {
      "title": "Teaching Fellow - Foundation Science",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-12\nFull time\n\nFoundation Science Teaching Fellow | School of Health Science and Clinical Practice | Full-time | Torrens University Australia Help shape the future of higher education. At Torrens University Australia, we're redefining what learning looks like.    We're building a new cohort of Teaching Fellows - innovative, student-focused academics who are passionate about creating engaging learning experiences and helping shape the next generation of teaching and learning.    This is more than a teaching role. You'll join a team leading the evolution of higher education through student-centred learning, AI-enabled teaching, digital innovation, and contemporary learning design. Why this role? This role has been created to strengthen Torrens University’s permanent academic workforce, supporting the delivery of flexible, high-quality, student-centred learning experiences across on-campus, online, hybrid and asynchronous learning environments, while enhancing student success and employability.    We're looking for educators who don't simply teach, they innovate.    People who are excited by questions like:  • How can AI enhance learning?  • What does great online teaching look like?  • How can data and student feedback improve the learning experience?  • How do we prepare graduates for careers that don't yet exist? About the role As a Teaching Fellow, you’ll join the School of Health Science and Clinical Practice, inspiring and supporting the next generation of health professionals. You’ll teach across our Diploma, Bachelor’s and Master’s Health Science programs, with a focus on Foundation Sciences, including Anatomy and Physiology, Healthcare in the Digital World, Evidence-Based Practice, Critical Literature Review, Pathophysiology and Clinical Assessment. You’ll also contribute to curriculum development, subject review and continuous improvement across the Health Science programs. This includes designing contemporary learning activities, developing innovative assessment approaches and ensuring curriculum remains relevant, inclusive and aligned with student and industry needs. Contribute to curriculum development: Support the design, review and continuous improvement of subjects, learning resources and curriculum activities. Innovate in assessment: Design authentic, inclusive and engaging assessment activities that support learning, demonstrate student capability and promote employability. Engage in scholarship: Contribute to scholarship of teaching and learning by evaluating teaching practices, sharing insights and applying evidence to improve student outcomes.   You'll combine outstanding teaching practice with digital capability, learning design and innovation to create learning experiences that are flexible, engaging and centred around student success. What you'll be doing - review Job description for full details    We're looking for educators who… Put students first: You create inclusive, engaging learning experiences and genuinely care about helping every student succeed.  Embrace innovation: You're curious about new technologies, confident experimenting with AI and digital tools, and willing to rethink traditional approaches to teaching.  Use evidence to improve: You seek feedback, use learning analytics and continuously refine your teaching based on what works.  Collaborate: You enjoy working with colleagues across disciplines to improve learning, share ideas, and solve challenges together.  Thrive in change: You're adaptable, resilient, and excited by working in a dynamic, digitally evolving higher education environment. This is a full-time, permanent position based at the Wakefield Campus in Adelaide. What you'll bring MSc, PhD, or equivalent qualification in a relevant discipline. A relevant postgraduate qualification, such as master's degree, PhD or equivalent, in health sciences, healthcare, education or a related discipline. Relevant academic, teaching, research or professional experience in health sciences, healthcare, biomedical science, allied health, nursing, public health or a related discipline, with the ability to apply contemporary knowledge to teaching and student learning. Strong facilitation skills across online and face-to-face learning environments Experience using learning technologies and digital tools to enhance teaching Confidence using, or enthusiasm for adopting, AI-enabled approaches in education Experience designing engaging learning and assessment activities A student-centred approach to teaching and learning Strong communication and collaboration skills A growth mindset and commitment to continuous professional learning How to Apply - Our recruitment process is different There is no prescribed format for your application. We encourage you to submit your application in the format that best showcases your experience, teaching philosophy and suitability for the role.    In addition to your CV, explain a concept relevant to your discipline in 5 minutes through activity-based learning. We would like to understand your facilitation style, impact and capability.     Recommended maximum length:   • Video: Up to 5 minutes   • Presentation or digital portfolio: Up to 5 slides/pages     Your application should demonstrate your teaching philosophy, student-centred approach, use of digital technologies and AI, innovation, continuous improvement, and the impact you've had on student outcomes. Why join Torrens? Join an institution committed to transforming education through innovation, technology and exceptional student experiences. You'll help shape the future of higher education while working alongside innovative educators committed to student success. Applications close: 10th December 2026 We will be reviewing applications as they are received. Interviews are expected to commence in early December 2026, with successful candidates anticipated to commence on 18th January 2027.    Application Process: Review > Interview(s) > Reference & Background Checks > Offer    Should you have accessibility requirements or needs please contact maur.bell@torrens.edu.au   for confidential support to ensure an equitable, barrier free application process as we have a Reasonable Adjustment Procedure in place to support you through the recruitment process. If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Wakefield/Teaching-Fellow---Nutrition_R31503-1": {
      "title": "Teaching Fellow - Nutrition",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-12\nFull time\n\nNutrition Teaching Fellow | School of Health Science and Clinical Practice | Full-time | Torrens University Australia Help shape the future of higher education. At Torrens University Australia, we're redefining what learning looks like.    We're building a new cohort of Teaching Fellows - innovative, student-focused academics who are passionate about creating engaging learning experiences and helping shape the next generation of teaching and learning.    This is more than a teaching role. You'll join a team leading the evolution of higher education through student-centred learning, AI-enabled teaching, digital innovation, and contemporary learning design. Why this role? This role has been created to strengthen Torrens University’s permanent academic workforce, supporting the delivery of flexible, high-quality, student-centred learning experiences across on-campus, online, hybrid and asynchronous learning environments, while enhancing student success and employability.    We're looking for educators who don't simply teach, they innovate.    People who are excited by questions like:  • How can AI enhance learning?  • What does great online teaching look like?  • How can data and student feedback improve the learning experience?  • How do we prepare graduates for careers that don't yet exist? About the role As a Teaching Fellow (Nutrition), you’ll join the School of Health Science and Clinical Practice, delivering engaging learning experiences across the Diploma and Bachelor of Health Science programs. You’ll focus on subjects including Health Education and Communication, Food Science, Systems and Policy, Diet and Disease, and Public Health Nutrition.   You'll combine outstanding teaching practice with digital capability, learning design and innovation to create learning experiences that are flexible, engaging and centred around student success. What you'll be doing - review Job description for full details    We're looking for educators who… Put students first: You create inclusive, engaging learning experiences and genuinely care about helping every student succeed.  Embrace innovation: You're curious about new technologies, confident experimenting with AI and digital tools, and willing to rethink traditional approaches to teaching.  Use evidence to improve: You seek feedback, use learning analytics and continuously refine your teaching based on what works.  Collaborate: You enjoy working with colleagues across disciplines to improve learning, share ideas, and solve challenges together.  Thrive in change: You're adaptable, resilient, and excited by working in a dynamic, digitally evolving higher education environment. This is a full-time, permanent position based at the Wakefield Campus in Adelaide. What you'll bring Postgraduate qualification in Nutrition (Master's degree or higher); a PhD (completed or in progress) is highly regarded. Current membership with a relevant professional association, together with contemporary professional experience in the nutrition field and the ability to maintain active industry engagement alongside the role. Demonstrated experience in the healthcare sector, with the ability to apply industry knowledge to teaching and student learning. Strong facilitation skills across online and face-to-face learning environments Experience using learning technologies and digital tools to enhance teaching Confidence using, or enthusiasm for adopting, AI-enabled approaches in education Experience designing engaging learning and assessment activities A student-centred approach to teaching and learning Strong communication and collaboration skills A growth mindset and commitment to continuous professional learning Relevant postgraduate qualifications (or working towards completion) How to Apply - Our recruitment process is different There is no prescribed format for your application. We encourage you to submit your application in the format that best showcases your experience, teaching philosophy and suitability for the role.    In addition to your CV, you may submit a short video, digital portfolio, presentation, personal website or another format that best represents you. Content matters more than creativity. We're interested in your teaching approach, impact, and capability—not production quality.   Recommended maximum length:   • Video: Up to 5 minutes   • Presentation or digital portfolio: Up to 5 slides/pages     Your application should demonstrate your teaching philosophy, student-centred approach, use of digital technologies and AI, innovation, continuous improvement, and the impact you've had on student outcomes.  Why join Torrens? Join an institution committed to transforming education through innovation, technology and exceptional student experiences. You'll help shape the future of higher education while working alongside innovative educators committed to student success. Applications close: 10th December 2026 We will be reviewing applications as they are received. Interviews are expected to commence in early December 2026, with successful candidates anticipated to commence on 18th January 2027.    Application Process: Review > Interview(s) > Reference & Background Checks > Offer    Should you have accessibility requirements or needs please contact maur.bell@torrens.edu.au   for confidential support to ensure an equitable, barrier free application process as we have a Reasonable Adjustment Procedure in place to support you through the recruitment process. If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Surry-Hills/Dean----School-of-Health-Sciences---Clinical-Practice_R31492-1": {
      "title": "Dean -  School of Health Sciences & Clinical Practice",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-12\nFull time\n\nWho we are:   At Torrens University Australia , making a difference is in our DNA. As a Certified B Corporation, we belong to a global community of future-focused companies using business as a force for good. We believe in the transformative power of education to change lives, families, communities – and the world. That’s why we’re on a mission to increase access to higher education, so learners from all walks of life can chase their dreams.    A progressive university, we ground our studies in industry. Expert academics bring their insights into the classroom, with a range of assessment types that aim to be authentic and informed by industry needs. Bridging the gap between study and work, our educators prepare students for career success and connect them with future employers. Building relevant skills, experience and networks from day one, students don’t just learn about their industry, they live it.    What’s the job?   As Dean of the School of Health Sciences & Clinical Practice , you will be the senior academic and operational leader of the School, responsible for driving academic excellence, student success, industry engagement, innovation, growth and operational performance across its portfolio. Reporting to the Provost and Deputy Vice Chancellor Academic, you will lead the School in alignment with the University’s strategic direction, objectives and key performance indicators. You will oversee learning and teaching, academic quality, curriculum innovation, student experience, workforce capability, partnerships, financial sustainability and growth. You will lead a high-performing, industry-connected and student-centred School that delivers outstanding educational outcomes through innovative pedagogy, digitally enabled learning, authentic assessment and contemporary workforce-aligned curriculum. This is an exciting opportunity to help shape the future of higher education at Torrens University Australia. As the higher education ecosystem continues to evolve, you will be at the forefront of new and innovative approaches to teaching and learning. You will have the opportunity to build on the School’s existing identity, contribute to its continued growth and help shape its next chapter. This is a role for someone who is open to new ideas, embraces innovation and is excited to guide meaningful development and change.   Principle accountabilities (but not limited to): Strategic Leadership and Academic Quality Learning, Teaching and Curriculum Innovation Student Success and Experience Industry Engagement and External Partnerships Financial and Operational Leadership  Research, Scholarship and Innovation  People Leadership and Organisational Capability  Who you are - Criteria: 1. An experienced senior academic leader with a strong record in higher education or a multi-sector education environment, including responsibility for academic delivery, quality, student outcomes and operational performance. 2. You hold an earned doctorate and have academic standing appropriate for appointment at Professorial level, with demonstrated credibility in learning and teaching, academic governance and curriculum innovation. 3. You have a strong understanding of the Australian higher education regulatory environment, including TEQSA, the Higher Education Standards Framework, ESOS obligations and relevant professional accreditation requirements. 4. You have experience leading online, digitally enabled and multi-campus education, with a strong understanding of contemporary pedagogy, workforce-aligned curriculum and integrated higher education and vocational education pathways. 5. You bring experience managing complex academic operations, budgets, workforce planning, organisational change and industry partnerships that support employability and student outcomes. 6. You are an inspirational, inclusive and collaborative leader with strong communication, influencing and stakeholder engagement skills, a commitment to equity and inclusion, and a clear focus on student success and institutional impact. 7. Relevant qualifications or experience in health sciences, clinical practice or a related discipline would be highly regarded. Please submit your resume and a cover letter addressing the seven criteria outlined above. To read more about the role please click here . This is a permanent full-time position based at one of our Campus locations in Brisbane, Sydney, Melbourne and Adelaide.  Why join us?   Bold, modern and agile, we are Australia's fastest-growing university, going from 164 students in 2014 to 40,000+ alumni across 115+ countries and 2,000+ staff today. In 2020, Australian Financial Review named us one of the country's most innovative companies. As we continue to establish ourselves as a truly global university, we never lose sight of our student-centric approach. Supported by teams of passionate people, you will find opportunities for professional development and career progression. We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer and committed to creating an inclusive workplace. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, colour, religion, age, ethnicity, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, or any other protected characteristic. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all positions. Hiring process   Please submit your resume and a cover letter addressing the seven criteria outlined above. We aim to provide you with the information you need at each stage of this process to help you present your best self. If you have any accessibility requirements, please contact your recruiter at maur.bell@torrens.edu.au for confidential support. We are committed to ensuring an equitable, barrier-free application process and have a Reasonable Adjustment Procedure in place to support you throughout the recruitment process. To learn more about what makes Torrens University Australia a great place to work, visit https://www.torrens.edu.au/blog .    We’d love to hear from you. Job reference: R31492 To ensure a fair and thorough review process, applications for this role will close on 9th December 2026. If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Flinders/Talent-Acquisition-Advisor_R31522-1": {
      "title": "Talent Acquisition Advisor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-13\nFull time\n\nWho we are? At Torrens University Australia, making a difference is in our DNA. As a Certified B Corporation, we belong to a global community of future-focused companies using business as a force for good. We believe in the transformative power of education to change lives, families, communities – and the world. That’s why we’re on a mission to increase access to higher education, so learners from all walks of life can chase their dreams. Just like our students, our employees are a diverse group who want to make an impact. When you join us, we give you the freedom to be bold, creative and courageous – with flexible working arrangements that allow you to bring your best. We’ve built a culture that celebrates community, collaboration and innovation, where people love what they do . About the role: Reporting to the Talent Acquisition Manager, the Talent Acquisition Advisor will lead end-to-end recruitment processes in partnership with hiring managers across Torrens Global Education.   You will provide practical recruitment advice, coordinate hiring activity and deliver a positive experience for candidates and stakeholders. Alongside day-to-day recruitment, you will manage and contribute to projects within Talent Acquisition and across the wider People and Talent team. The role combines recruitment delivery, stakeholder management, candidate care, reporting, project coordination and continuous improvement of talent acquisition processes. What you’ll do: Partner with hiring managers to understand recruitment needs and provide practical advice throughout the process. Coordinate recruitment activity from job creation through to appointment, including interview scheduling, candidate communication and recruitment administration. Support the development and review of position descriptions and job advertisements. Write and post engaging job advertisements across relevant channels. Conduct phone screens and provide candidate assessments, summaries and recommendations. Develop behavioural and competency-based interview questions in partnership with hiring managers. Participate in interview panels and provide informed candidate recommendations. Conduct reference checks and provide advice on candidate suitability, development areas and recommendations. Maintain accurate candidate records and recruitment activity in the applicant tracking system. Provide a high level of candidate care, including responding to queries and providing feedback. Assist with recruitment reporting, HR metrics and process improvement initiatives. Support recruitment projects and maintain recruitment guidance for the intranet. Assist with recruitment administration, including agency invoices, charge rates, contracts and terms of business. Act as a super user of the recruitment system and support hiring managers with its use. Lead and contribute to Talent Acquisition projects and process improvement initiatives. Collaborate on projects across the wider People and Talent team. Support the implementation of initiatives that improve recruitment processes, systems and stakeholder experience. About you: You will be an organised and service-focused recruitment professional with experience managing end-to-end recruitment processes. You will be confident working with a range of stakeholders and able to manage multiple priorities while maintaining a high level of attention to detail. You will also bring: Previous experience in end-to-end recruitment. Strong communication and relationship management skills. A positive, practical and customer-focused approach. Excellent organisation, time management and multitasking skills. Strong attention to detail and administrative capability. Experience using recruitment or applicant tracking systems, preferably. A basic understanding of employment legislation, Modern Awards and relevant state-based requirements. Strong computer literacy, including Microsoft Word, PowerPoint and Excel. Experience using an applicant tracking system (ATS); Workday experience is advantageous. To view the job description, please click here .   This is a full-time, six-month fixed-term contract based at our Flinders Street campus in Melbourne, with the potential for the role to become permanent. Why join us? Bold, modern and agile, we’re Australia’s fastest-growing university, going from 164 students in 2014 to 40,000+ alumni across 115+ countries and 2000+ staff today. In 2020, Australian Financial Review named us one of the country’s most innovative companies. As we continue to establish ourselves as a truly global university, we never lose sight of our student-centric approach. Supported by teams of passionate people, you’ll find endless opportunities for professional development and career progression.   We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer and committed to creating an inclusive workplace. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, colour, religion, age, ethnicity, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, or any other protected characteristic.   We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all positions. What we offer: We support your personal passions, development and wellbeing, to make your working life a more rewarding experience. At Torrens University Australia, you’ll benefit from:     Study free in a course/degree related to your position     Access to internal opportunities - Be supported to learn, grow and move across the organisation A collaborative, purpose-driven working environment where your work can make a meaningful difference Hiring process: We aim to provide you with the information you need at each stage of this process to help you present your best self.   If you have any accessibility requirements, please contact your recruiter at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au for confidential support. We are committed to ensuring an equitable, barrier-free application process and have a Reasonable Adjustment Procedure in place to support you throughout the recruitment process. To learn more about what makes Torrens University Australia a great place to work, visit https://www.torrens.edu.au/blog . We’d love to hear from you.   Important information We are seeking someone who is available to commence immediately. Applications will be reviewed as they are received, and the advertisement may close earlier if a suitable candidate is identified. Applications close Friday, 11 December 2026, unless the position is filled sooner. Applicants must have ongoing, unrestricted working rights in Australia. If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Brisbane/Teaching-Fellow---Nursing--Brisbane-_R31523-1": {
      "title": "Teaching Fellow - Nursing (Brisbane)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-13\nFull time\n\nNursing Teaching Fellow | School of Health Science and Clinical Practice | Full-time | Torrens University Australia Help shape the future of higher education. At Torrens University Australia, we're redefining what learning looks like.    We're building a new cohort of Teaching Fellows - innovative, student-focused academics who are passionate about creating engaging learning experiences and helping shape the next generation of teaching and learning.    This is more than a teaching role. You'll join a team leading the evolution of higher education through student-centred learning, AI-enabled teaching, digital innovation, and contemporary learning design.  Why this role?  This role has been created to strengthen Torrens University’s permanent academic workforce, supporting the delivery of flexible, high-quality, student-centred learning experiences across on-campus, online, hybrid and asynchronous learning environments, while enhancing student success and employability.    We're looking for educators who don't simply teach, they innovate.    People who are excited by questions like:   • How can AI enhance learning?  • What does great online teaching look like?  • How can data and student feedback improve the learning experience?  • How do we prepare graduates for careers that don't yet exist?  About the role  As a Teaching Fellow, you’ll join the School of Health Science and Clinical Practice, inspiring and supporting the next generation of nursing professionals. You’ll teach across our Bachelor of Nursing subjects.  You'll combine outstanding teaching practice with digital capability, learning design and innovation to create learning experiences that are flexible, engaging and centred around student success.   What you'll be doing - review Job description for full details    We're looking for educators who…  Put students first: You create inclusive, engaging learning experiences and genuinely care about helping every student succeed.  Embrace innovation: You're curious about new technologies, confident experimenting with AI and digital tools, and willing to rethink traditional approaches to teaching.  Use evidence to improve: You seek feedback, use learning analytics and continuously refine your teaching based on what works.  Collaborate: You enjoy working with colleagues across disciplines to improve learning, share ideas, and solve challenges together.  Thrive in change: You're adaptable, resilient, and excited by working in a dynamic, digitally evolving higher education environment.  These are full-time, permanent positions, with one role available in Adelaide and one in Brisbane.  What you'll bring  MSc, PhD, or equivalent qualification in a relevant discipline  Demonstrated current clinical experience in the nursing, with the ability to apply industry knowledge to teaching and student learning  Strong facilitation skills across online and face-to-face learning environments in Higher Education  Experience using learning technologies and digital tools to enhance teaching  Confidence using, or enthusiasm for adopting, AI-enabled approaches in education  Experience designing engaging learning and assessment activities  A student-centred approach to teaching and learning  Strong communication and collaboration skills  A growth mindset and commitment to continuous professional learning  Relevant postgraduate qualifications (or working towards completion) How to Apply - Our recruitment process is different   There is no prescribed format for your application. We encourage you to submit your application in the format that best showcases your experience, teaching philosophy and suitability for the role.    In addition to your CV, you may submit a short video, digital portfolio, presentation, personal website or another format that best represents you. Content matters more than creativity. We're interested in your teaching approach, impact, and capability—not production quality.   Recommended maximum length:   • Video: Up to 5 minutes   • Presentation or digital portfolio: Up to 5 slides/pages     Your application should demonstrate your teaching philosophy, student-centred approach, use of digital technologies and AI, innovation, continuous improvement, and the impact you've had on student outcomes.  Why join Torrens?  Join an institution committed to transforming education through innovation, technology and exceptional student experiences. You'll help shape the future of higher education while working alongside innovative educators committed to student success.  Applications close: 10th December 2026  We will be reviewing applications as they are received.  Interviews are expected to commence in early December 2026, with successful candidates anticipated to commence on 18th January 2027.    Application Process: Review > Interview(s) > Reference & Background Checks > Offer    Should you have accessibility requirements or needs please contact maur.bell@torrens.edu.au  for confidential support to ensure an equitable, barrier free application process as we have a Reasonable Adjustment Procedure in place to support you through the recruitment process.  If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Wakefield/Student-Services-Team-Leader--Digital-_R31478": {
      "title": "Student Services Team Leader (Digital)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-20\nFull time\n\nStudent Services Team Leader Permanent full-time | Adelaide, Melbourne, Sydney or Brisbane Who we are At Torrens University Australia, making a difference is in our DNA. We believe in the transformative power of education to change lives, families, communities—and the world. That’s why we’re on a mission to increase access to higher education, so learners from all walks of life can chase their dreams.  Just like our students, our employees are a diverse group who want to make an impact. When you join us, we give you the freedom to be bold, creative and courageous, with flexible working arrangements that allow you to bring your best. We’ve built a culture that celebrates community, collaboration and innovation, where people love what they do. What’s the job?   As the Student Services Team Leader, you’ll lead a team of Student Services Advisors and help deliver an exceptional service experience to students across phone, email and chat.  You’ll support the team to meet service targets, resolve student enquiries accurately and efficiently, and provide a consistent experience to new and existing students.  This role is responsible for team leadership, coaching, performance, workforce planning and continuous improvement. You’ll also support the Student Services Manager with new processes and help build a respectful, collaborative and high-performing team culture.  This is a permanent full-time opportunity that can be based at any of our Australian locations: Adelaide, Melbourne, Sydney or Brisbane.  Principal accountabilities include, but are not limited to:   1. Team leadership   Lead, support and develop a high-performing team through regular communication, coaching, mentoring, feedback and performance management. Support recruitment, professional development, team engagement and workforce planning.  2. Student service delivery   Support the team to respond to student enquiries across phone, email and chat. Ensure enquiries are resolved within agreed service levels, complex matters are escalated appropriately and student interactions are accurately recorded.  3. Performance and continuous improvement   Monitor team performance against customer service targets and service levels. Identify opportunities to improve processes, systems and the student experience, and support the implementation of new procedures.  4. Collaboration and stakeholder support   Build effective relationships across Student Services and the wider University. Contribute to projects, team activities, Orientation and Information Sessions, and support initiatives that improve collaboration, retention and student outcomes.  Who you are   You are an experienced student or customer service professional with strong leadership skills and a passion for delivering high-quality service.  You will ideally have:  At least three to four years’ experience in student services, customer service, administration or a related area.  Previous experience leading, supervising or developing a team.  Experience managing performance, service levels and customer experience targets.  Strong communication and interpersonal skills.  The ability to coach, mentor and motivate team members.  Strong problem-solving and decision-making skills.  The ability to manage complex enquiries and escalate matters appropriately.  Experience identifying and implementing process improvements.  Strong organisational skills and the ability to manage competing priorities.  The ability to work across multiple systems in a fast-paced environment.  A proactive, reliable and detail-focused approach.  A strong commitment to collaboration, accountability and service excellence.  This role may require work outside of ordinary working hours and rotating weekends, in line with business requirements.  To read more about the role, please click here . Why join us?   Bold, modern and agile, we’re Australia’s fastest-growing university, growing from 164 students in 2014 to more than 40,000 alumni across 115+ countries and 2,000+ staff today.  In 2020, the Australian Financial Review named us one of the country’s most innovative companies. As we continue to establish ourselves as a truly global university, we never lose sight of our student-centred approach. Supported by teams of passionate people, you’ll find opportunities for professional development and career progression.  We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer and committed to creating an inclusive workplace. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, colour, religion, age, ethnicity, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability or any other protected characteristic.  We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all positions.  What we offer   We support your personal passions, development and wellbeing to make your working life a more rewarding experience. At Torrens University Australia, you’ll benefit from:  Study free in a course or degree related to your position  Access to internal opportunities—be supported to learn, grow and move across the organisation  A values-driven and purpose-led working environment  Hiring process   We aim to provide you with the information you need at each stage of the process to help you present your best self.  If you have any accessibility requirements, please contact us at Sebastian.pabon@torrens.edu.au for confidential support. We are committed to ensuring an equitable, barrier-free application process and have a Reasonable Adjustment Procedure in place to support you throughout the recruitment process.  To learn more about what makes Torrens University Australia a great place to work, visit https://www.torrens.edu.au/blog .  We’d love to hear from you.  Please note that we may close applications earlier if a suitable candidate is identified. You can expect to hear from our Talent Acquisition team after this date with updates regarding your application.  Applications will be reviewed as they are received, and the advertisement may close before the advertised closing date if a suitable candidate is identified.  If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Flinders/Marketing-Executive_R31512": {
      "title": "Marketing Executive",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-20\nPart time\n\nMarketing Executive   12-month fixed-term contract until December 2027 | Full-time or 4 days per week | Hybrid Who we are   At Torrens University Australia, making a difference is in our DNA. We believe in the transformative power of education to change lives, families, communities—and the world. That’s why we’re on a mission to increase access to higher education, so learners from all walks of life can chase their dreams.  Just like our students, our employees are a diverse group who want to make an impact. When you join us, we give you the freedom to be bold, creative and courageous, with flexible working arrangements that allow you to bring your best. We’ve built a culture that celebrates community, collaboration and innovation, where people love what they do.  What’s the job?   As a Marketing Executive, you’ll play a key role in developing and executing integrated marketing campaigns that drive awareness, consideration and applications for our School of Technology.  Working across advertising, digital, social media, direct marketing, experiential activities, events and collateral development, you’ll deliver compelling campaigns that strengthen our brand and support the University’s strategic growth.  Working closely with faculty, internal stakeholders and agency partners, you’ll execute campaigns across digital advertising, social media, websites, events and video. This is an exciting opportunity for a hands-on marketer who enjoys balancing creativity with data-driven decision-making in a fast-paced environment.  If you’re passionate about creating impactful campaigns and helping transform lives through education, we’d love to hear from you.  This is a 12-month fixed-term contract through to December 2027. The role is available on either a full-time basis, working 40 hours per week, or four days per week, working 30.4 hours per week.  The role offers hybrid working arrangements, with an expectation of attending campus two to three days per week. The successful candidate will preferably be based in Melbourne or Adelaide. The role can be based at either our Surry Hills or Flinders campus.  Principal accountabilities include, but are not limited to:   Campaign development and content   Develop and execute integrated paid marketing campaigns   Create engaging marketing content across video, social and blogs  Campaign coordination and collaboration   Manage campaign briefs, timelines and creative delivery with internal teams and external agencies.   Collaborate with stakeholders across marketing, sales, faculty and student services.  Campaign performance and reporting   Monitor campaign performance and recommend optimisations using data and market insights.   Produce campaign reports and contribute insights that improve future marketing performance.  Marketing assets and events   Maintain marketing assets including websites, print, campaign landing pages and sales conversion resources.   Coordinate logistics for Open Days, Information Sessions and other recruitment events.  Who you are   A marketing professional with a relevant marketing qualification and at least two years’ proven marketing experience—ideally within a technology or education organisation.  You have experience across the marketing mix, including campaign planning, audience segmentation, digital marketing, social media, direct marketing, events and content development.  You have experience developing and executing social media and lead generation campaigns, ideally within a consumer-focused or youth-oriented industry.  You are confident managing multiple campaigns, projects, deadlines, agencies, suppliers and internal stakeholders in a fast-paced environment.  You have strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to develop clear, engaging and audience-focused marketing content.  You are comfortable using data and campaign insights to guide decision-making, evaluate performance and recommend optimisation opportunities.  You are creative, accurate, organised and self-motivated, with strong attention to detail and the ability to manage your workload independently.  Experience with Salesforce, campaign reporting, marketing automation or education marketing would be advantageous.  To read more about the role, please click here .  Why join us?   Bold, modern and agile, we’re Australia’s fastest-growing university, growing from 164 students in 2014 to more than 40,000 alumni across 115+ countries and 2,000+ staff today.  In 2020, the Australian Financial Review named us one of the country’s most innovative companies. As we continue to establish ourselves as a truly global university, we never lose sight of our student-centred approach.  Supported by teams of passionate people, you’ll find opportunities for professional development and career progression.  We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer and committed to creating an inclusive workplace. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, colour, religion, age, ethnicity, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability or any other protected characteristic.  We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all positions.  What we offer   We support your personal passions, development and wellbeing to make your working life a more rewarding experience. At Torrens University Australia, you’ll benefit from:  Study free in a course or degree related to your position  Access to internal opportunities—be supported to learn, grow and move across the organisation  A values-driven and purpose-led working environment  Hiring process   We aim to provide you with the information you need at each stage of the process to help you present your best self.  If you have any accessibility requirements, please contact us at Sebastian.pabon@torrens.edu.au for confidential support. We are committed to ensuring an equitable, barrier-free application process and have a Reasonable Adjustment Procedure in place to support you throughout the recruitment process.  To learn more about what makes Torrens University Australia a great place to work, visit https://www.torrens.edu.au/blog .  We’d love to hear from you.  Please note that we may close applications earlier if a suitable candidate is identified. You can expect to hear from our Talent Acquisition team after this date with updates regarding your application. Applications will be reviewed as they are received, and the advertisement may close before the advertised closing date if a suitable candidate is identified. If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Brisbane/Industry-Consultant_R31324": {
      "title": "Industry Consultant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-18\nFull time\n\nIndustry Consultant – Business & Technology   Permanent Full-Time | Brisbane | Face-to-Face / Hybrid   Who we are   At Torrens University Australia, making a difference is in our DNA. We believe in the transformative power of education to change lives, families, communities and the world.  That’s why we’re on a mission to increase access to higher education and create learning experiences that prepare students for real careers and real opportunities.  Our people are a diverse group who want to make an impact. When you join us, you’ll be encouraged to think boldly, build connections and turn ideas into outcomes. We’ve created a culture centred on collaboration, innovation and making a meaningful difference for our students.  What’s the job?   Industry engagement is central to how we prepare our students for the workforce.   As our Industry Consultant – Business & Technology , you will be the connection between Torrens University and the organisations, employers and industry leaders who can create real-world opportunities for our students and graduates.  You will develop, grow and manage industry partnerships across our school portfolios, securing Work Integrated Learning (WIL), internships, live briefs, industry projects and employment opportunities .  This is a highly commercial and relationship-driven role. You’ll spend your time connecting with employers, understanding workforce needs, developing new partnerships and identifying opportunities where industry and education can create value together.  You won’t simply maintain relationships — you’ll create opportunities .  This role is based at our Fortitude Valley campus in Brisbane and requires regular face-to-face engagement with colleagues, students and industry partners. Hybrid working is available for part of the week, however this is not a fully remote position .   Key points about this role   Build & Grow Industry Partnerships: Develop trusted relationships across Business, Technology and professional sectors, turning conversations into long-term partnerships and opportunities.  Create Real Career Opportunities: Secure internships, WIL placements, live briefs, projects and employment pathways that give students meaningful industry experience.  Drive Business Development: Identify new organisations, partnership opportunities and B2B/B2B2C connections that expand Torrens University's industry ecosystem.  Connect Industry Across Torrens: Bring employers together with Academics, Employability, Careers, Alumni and other teams to create mutually beneficial initiatives.  Track Outcomes & Improve Performance: Maintain strong CRM discipline, monitor partnership and placement outcomes, and use insights to continuously strengthen industry engagement.  Who you are   A Natural Relationship Builder: You know how to create credibility quickly, build professional networks and maintain strong relationships with senior stakeholders and employers.  Commercial & Opportunity Focused: You naturally identify opportunities, open doors and turn industry conversations into tangible partnerships and outcomes.  Experienced in Relevant Industries: You bring strong experience across Business, Technology, professional services or a related sector and understand workforce and employer needs.  Recruitment, Partnerships or Business Development Experienced: Your background may include recruitment, early careers, employer engagement, business development, partnerships, L&D or a similar relationship-focused environment.  Confident, Independent & Outcomes Driven: You are comfortable owning a portfolio, working independently, attending industry events and collaborating across multiple internal teams to get results.  Experience securing internships, placements, employment opportunities or other industry-based learning experiences will be highly regarded.  A relevant tertiary qualification, industry certification or equivalent combination of experience and training would be advantageous.  Eligibility requirements   To be considered for this opportunity, you must:  Be currently located in Australia   Hold full working rights in Australia   Be able to regularly attend our Fortitude Valley campus in Brisbane   Be available to undertake face-to-face meetings, industry visits and events as required  Why join us?   Bold, modern and agile, Torrens University Australia has grown from 164 students in 2014 to a global community of more than 40,000 alumni across 115+ countries.  Our focus remains firmly on preparing students for real life beyond university.  This role gives you a genuine opportunity to influence that outcome — building the partnerships, networks and employment pathways that connect education with industry.  You’ll work across a broad external network while collaborating with passionate teams across Employability, Academics, Careers, Alumni and the wider university.  We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer and are committed to creating an inclusive workplace. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples and welcome applicants from diverse backgrounds and experiences.  What we offer   At Torrens University Australia, we support your development, wellbeing and career ambitions.  You’ll benefit from:  The opportunity to study a course or degree related to your position at no tuition cost  Access to internal career opportunities across the organisation  Professional development and learning opportunities  A purpose-led and values-driven working environment  Hybrid working opportunities alongside the face-to-face requirements of the role  The opportunity to directly influence student employability and industry outcomes  Hiring process   We aim to provide you with the information you need at each stage of the recruitment process so you can present your best self.  If you have any accessibility requirements, please contact Sebastian.pabon@torrens.edu.au for confidential support. We are committed to ensuring an equitable, barrier-free application process and have a Reasonable Adjustment Procedure in place to support you throughout recruitment.   Applications and recruitment timeline   Applications will remain open for four weeks and will close on Wednesday, 16 December 2026 .  However, we will be actively reviewing applications, speaking with candidates and progressing the recruitment process as suitable candidates apply . We encourage you to apply early rather than waiting until the closing date.  Torrens University Australia will enter its end-of-year shutdown period from 18 December 2026 to 4 January 2027 . Recruitment communication may pause during this period and will resume following the shutdown.  The anticipated commencement date for the successful candidate is 4 January or 11 January 2027 , depending on availability and completion of the recruitment process.  Please note that we may close applications earlier if a suitable candidate is identified.  To learn more about what makes Torrens University Australia a great place to work, visit our Torrens University website and blog.  We’d love to hear from you.   Job reference: R31324   If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Surry-Hills/Information-Security-Engineer_R30763-1": {
      "title": "Information Security Engineer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-18\nFull time\n\nWho we are?   At Torrens University Australia,  making a difference is in our DNA. As a Certified B Corporation, we belong to a global community of future-focused companies using business as a force for good. We believe in the transformative power of education to change lives, families, communities – and the world. That’s why we’re on a mission to increase access to higher education, so learners from all walks of life can chase their dreams.     Just like our students, our employees are a diverse group who want to make an impact. When you join us, we give you the freedom to be bold, creative, and courageous – with flexible working arrangements that allow you to bring your best. We’ve built a culture that celebrates community, collaboration, and innovation, where people love what they do .      What’s the job?   The Information Security Engineer is responsible for the overall Cyber security stance of Torrens institutions.  They should have a strong appreciation with demonstrated expertise regarding IT Security including continuous assessment of security posture and ongoing improvements.    Principal accountabilities include (but are not limited to):   The engineer will be a self-driven technologist who works closely with others within the security department as well as members of other Information Technology departments and business stakeholders to identify, analyze, and remediate threats.   The engineer may also be leveraged to assist in designing, building, operating and monitoring leading-edge security infrastructure, platforms, applications and tools to meet strategic and tactical security objectives.   The engineer will work with technical managers, software development, and IT operations staff to mitigate or remediate vulnerabilities and manage technology risks across the enterprise.   Conduct Vendor Security assessments for new vendors required by the business in a timely manner.  Monitor, analyze, and respond to potential security threats identified by Torrens security systems (e.g. Nexpose, Cisco AMP for Endpoints, Cisco IDS, email-based threats, Cisco Umbrella  Enter information into ticketing and similar systems to track threats, assignment, and remediation actions    Who you are   Bachelor's degree in computer science or engineering, Management Information Systems, or a related technical field  5+ years of combined hands-on experience in analysis and security engineering, research and/or consulting  5+ years of networking background; preferred experience with Cisco technologies  Experience understanding and determining vulnerabilities via industry standard tools  Experience monitoring and assessing security threats  Responsible for remediation or analysis for identified security incident  Understanding of enterprise, network, system/endpoint, and application-level security issues and risks    To read more about the role please  click here .    This is a permanent, full-time position with hybrid work flexibility. Preference to be based at our Surry Hills campus in Sydney but open also open to the role being based at locations where we have a campus – Melbourne, Brisbane & Adelaide.    Why join us?    Bold, modern and agile, we’re Australia’s fastest-growing university, going from 164 students in 2014 to 40,000+ alumni across 115+ countries and 2000+ staff today. In 2020,  Australian Financial Review  named us one of the country’s most innovative companies. As we continue to establish ourselves as a truly global university, we never lose sight of our student-centric approach. Supported by teams of passionate people, you’ll find endless opportunities for professional development and career progression.     We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer and committed to creating an inclusive workplace. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, colour, religion, age, ethnicity, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, or any other protected characteristic.     We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all positions.     What we offer:   We support your personal passions, development and wellbeing, to make your working life a more rewarding experience. At   Torrens University Australia, you’ll benefit from:      Study free in a course/degree related to your position      B Corp certified university – values driven, and purpose led  Access to internal opportunities - Be supported to learn, grow and move across the organisation          Hiring process    We aim to provide you with the information you need at each stage of this process to help you present your best self.     If you have any accessibility requirements, please contact your recruiter at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au for confidential support. We are committed to ensuring an equitable, barrier-free application process and have a Reasonable Adjustment Procedure in place to support you throughout the recruitment process.    To learn more about what makes Torrens University Australia a great place to work, visit  https://www.torrens.edu.au/blog .    We’d love to hear from you.    Job reference: R30763    Applications for this role will close on Wednesday 16 December.  Please note, we may close applications earlier should a suitable candidate be identified. You can expect to hear from our Talent Acquisition team after this date with updates regarding your application.   If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Brisbane/Course-Lead----Marketing-Analytics---Enterprise-_R31479": {
      "title": "Course Lead​ - Marketing Analytics & Enterprise​",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-17\nFull time\n\nWho we are?    At Torrens University Australia, making a difference is in our DNA. We believe in the transformative power of education to change lives, families, communities – and the world. That’s why we’re on a mission to increase access to higher education, so learners from all walks of life can chase their dreams.  Just like our students, our employees are a diverse group who want to make an impact. When you join us, we give you the freedom to be bold, creative, and courageous – with flexible working arrangements that allow you to bring your best. We’ve built a culture that celebrates community, collaboration, and innovation, where people love what they do.     What’s the job?   The Course Leader is an academic role within the School responsible for the day-to-day coordination, quality assurance and operational management of a designated course. You will help ensure students experience a high-quality, coherent and well-managed program of study from enrolment through to graduation. Reporting to the Discipline Head, you will provide course-level academic leadership and functional coordination of Subject Coordinators, academic staff and teaching teams. Working closely with the Discipline Head, Student Services and the Associate Dean Learning and Teaching, you will support consistent course delivery, student progression, subject quality and a positive student experience. You will also maintain an active teaching contribution and engage in scholarship and professional development appropriate to your academic classification.    Principle accountabilities: Manage day-to-day course planning, scheduling and delivery across trimesters, campuses and delivery modes, ensuring a consistent and high-quality student experience. Provide course-level academic leadership and coordination to Subject Coordinators, academic staff and sessional/casual teaching teams. Maintain oversight of academic quality, moderation, assessment consistency, course content and subject delivery in line with University standards. Monitor course performance, student progression, retention, success and satisfaction, using data and reporting to drive course-level improvements. Coordinate curriculum delivery, course and subject review processes, accreditation requirements and quality documentation including CCRs and SQRs. Support industry-engaged learning and employability through WIL, live briefs, placements, industry projects and other applied learning experiences. Act as a key academic point of contact for complex student queries, progression matters and academic support, escalating significant risks where required. Contribute to scholarship, professional practice, governance, compliance and risk management at the course level. Who you are:  You are an organised, student-focused academic leader who enjoys bringing together people, processes and academic standards to deliver a strong course experience. You can coordinate complex academic activity, provide clear guidance to teaching teams and use data and feedback to identify improvements. You communicate effectively with students, academics and professional teams, manage competing priorities with confidence and bring a collaborative, inclusive approach to course leadership. To be successful in this position you will have:  A relevant postgraduate qualification at doctoral or master’s level, or equivalent professional standing and academic experience in the discipline. Significant course coordination or academic leadership experience may also be considered. Relevant professional accreditation, registration or industry standing where applicable to the course. Demonstrated academic leadership experience in higher education, including course or subject coordination and functional leadership of academic and teaching teams. Experience in course delivery, quality assurance and student progression management in a higher education setting. Sound understanding of curriculum design, assessment, moderation, accreditation and higher education quality frameworks, including TEQSA, AQF and HESF. Experience using student data and feedback to inform course-level improvement and support student success. Demonstrated commitment to inclusive practice, positive student experience and culturally safe, student-centred delivery. Demonstrated contribution to scholarship, research and/or professional practice relevant to the discipline, with scholarly outputs appropriate to classification. Experience engaging with industry partners or professional bodies relevant to the course. Strong organisational, communication, stakeholder engagement and planning skills, with the ability to manage competing priorities and deadlines. To read more about the role please click here . This is a full-time, permanent position based at our Brisbane campus. Why join us?  Bold, modern and agile, we’re Australia’s fastest-growing university, going from 164 students in 2014 to 40,000+ alumni across 115+ countries and 2,000+ staff today. In 2020, Australian Financial Review named us one of the country’s most innovative companies. As we continue to establish ourselves as a truly global university, we never lose sight of our student-centric approach. Supported by teams of passionate people, you’ll find opportunities for professional development and career progression.    We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer and committed to creating an inclusive workplace. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, colour, religion, age, ethnicity, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, or any other protected characteristic.    We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all positions.    What we offer:  We support your personal passions, development and wellbeing, to make your working life a more rewarding experience. At Torrens University Australia, you’ll benefit from:  Study free in a course or degree related to your position  Access to internal opportunities – be supported to learn, grow and move across the organisation  A values-driven and purpose-led working environment  Hiring process:    We aim to provide you with the information you need at each stage of this process to help you present your best self.   If you have any accessibility requirements, please contact us at Sebastian.pabon@torrens.edu.au for confidential support. We are committed to ensuring an equitable, barrier-free application process and have a Reasonable Adjustment Procedure in place to support you throughout the recruitment process.  To learn more about what makes Torrens University Australia a great place to work, visit https://www.torrens.edu.au/blog .  We’d love to hear from you.  Job reference: R31479 Applications for this role will close on 15th December 2026.  Please note, we may close applications earlier should a suitable candidate be identified. You can expect to hear from our Talent Acquisition team after this date with updates regarding your application.  If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
