    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Surry-Hills/QA---Test-Analyst_R31592-1": {
      "title": "QA / Test Analyst",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-23\nFull time\n\nWho we are?   At Torrens University Australia, making a difference is in our DNA. As a Certified B Corporation, we belong to a global community of future-focused companies using business as a force for good. We believe in the transformative power of education to change lives, families, communities – and the world. That’s why we’re on a mission to increase access to higher education, so learners from all walks of life can chase their dreams.     Just like our students, our employees are a diverse group who want to make an impact. When you join us, we give you the freedom to be bold, creative, and courageous – with flexible working arrangements that allow you to bring your best. We’ve built a culture that celebrates community, collaboration, and innovation, where people love what they do .     What’s the job?   As QA/Test Analyst , you will safeguard the quality of Torrens University Australia’s digital experiences, experimentation program and production releases. Working within the Architecture & Engineering team and supporting the CRO & UX Team, you will ensure that experiments, website releases and tracking implementations are thoroughly tested before launch. You will help ensure that every test result can be trusted and that digital experiences are reliable, accessible and performant for our users. You will own and continuously improve QA processes, test plans, deployment checklists and quality standards across experimentation and Sitecore releases. Working closely with developers, designers, marketing and analytics teams, you will help maintain a high standard of quality while supporting an agile delivery environment.  Principal accountabilities include (but are not limited to): Plan and perform functional, integration, regression, cross-browser, cross-device and accessibility testing across digital platforms and connected systems. Test A/B and personalisation experiments, validating experiment variants, audience targeting, exclusion rules, goals, GA4 events, dataLayer integrity and overall data quality. Monitor live experiments and releases for defects, tracking issues, rendering problems, sample ratio mismatch and other anomalies. Support defect triage, retesting, releases, hotfixes and post-release verification, ensuring agreed QA gates and sign-offs are completed. Maintain and improve test plans, deployment checklists, test evidence, defect reports and QA standards. Work collaboratively with developers, designers, marketing, analytics and technical teams to identify risks early and improve automation, CI/CD testing, test environments and delivery processes. Who you are   You have at least three years’ experience in QA or test analysis for websites or digital products, ideally in high-traffic or lead-generation environments. You have experience testing A/B and personalisation experiments using platforms such as VWO, Optimizely, Adobe Target or similar, along with validating GA4, dataLayer and tag management implementations. You are confident conducting functional, regression, cross-browser, cross-device and accessibility testing, and preparing clear test plans and defect reports. You are familiar with Agile delivery practices and tools such as Jira. Experience with Sitecore, automated testing tools such as Playwright or Cypress, Git, CI/CD pipelines and release management would be advantageous. You understand the importance of privacy, consent, web performance and data integrity in digital experimentation. You are detail-oriented, collaborative and pragmatic, with the ability to balance quality, delivery speed and sound human judgement when using AI-assisted QA tools. To read more about the role please click here . This is a permanent, full-time role to be based at our Surry Hills campus in Sydney.   Why join us?   Bold, modern and agile, we’re Australia’s fastest-growing university, going from 164 students in 2014 to 40,000+ alumni across 115+ countries and 2000+ staff today. In 2020, Australian Financial Review named us one of the country’s most innovative companies. As we continue to establish ourselves as a truly global university, we never lose sight of our student-centric approach. Supported by teams of passionate people, you’ll find endless opportunities for professional development and career progression. We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer and committed to creating an inclusive workplace. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, colour, religion, age, ethnicity, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, or any other protected characteristic.  We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all positions.    What we offer:   We support your personal passions, development and wellbeing, to make your working life a more rewarding experience. At  Torrens University Australia, you’ll benefit from:     Study free in a course/degree related to your position     B Corp certified university – values driven, and purpose led Access to internal opportunities - Be supported to learn, grow and move across the organisation      Hiring process   We aim to provide you with the information you need at each stage of this process to help you present your best self.  If you have any accessibility requirements, please contact your recruiter at Nikeey.silwal@torrens.edu.au for confidential support. We are committed to ensuring an equitable, barrier-free application process and have a Reasonable Adjustment Procedure in place to support you throughout the recruitment process.   To learn more about what makes Torrens University Australia a great place to work, visit https://www.torrens.edu.au/blog .    We’d love to hear from you. Job reference:  R31592 Applications for this role will close on Monday 21st December. Please note, we may close applications earlier should a suitable candidate be identified. You can expect to hear from our Talent Acquisition team after this date with updates regarding your application.  Our office will be closed from 18th December and over the Christmas period, which may cause delays in processing your application. We kindly ask that you allow up to 3 additional weeks after the application closing date for any updates. If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Surry-Hills/Sitecore-Developer--Full-Stack-_R31591-1": {
      "title": "Sitecore Developer (Full Stack)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-23\nFull time\n\nWho we are?   At Torrens University Australia, making a difference is in our DNA. As a Certified B Corporation, we belong to a global community of future-focused companies using business as a force for good. We believe in the transformative power of education to change lives, families, communities – and the world. That’s why we’re on a mission to increase access to higher education, so learners from all walks of life can chase their dreams.     Just like our students, our employees are a diverse group who want to make an impact. When you join us, we give you the freedom to be bold, creative, and courageous – with flexible working arrangements that allow you to bring your best. We’ve built a culture that celebrates community, collaboration, and innovation, where people love what they do .     What’s the job?   As Sitecore Developer (Full Stack) , you will play a critical role in scaling and productionising digital experiences within Torrens University Australia’s in-house CRO & UX Team. Working within Architecture & Engineering and reporting to the Technical Lead (Sitecore), you will convert successful experiments into permanent production features, build reusable Sitecore components and support personalisation across the university’s digital experience platforms. You will work across Sitecore XP and emerging headless platforms, helping to develop robust, scalable and maintainable digital experiences that support conversion, lead generation and enrolment growth. You will also work closely with the CRO & UX Team, developers, designers and QA specialists to deliver high-quality solutions from experimentation through to production.  Principal accountabilities include (but are not limited to): Convert successful experiments and UX enhancements into scalable, maintainable production features, including reusable Sitecore XP components, templates, renderings and data sources. Develop headless and composable digital experiences using technologies such as JSS, Next.js, Content SDK, Experience Edge, GraphQL and the Pages editor. Build and support personalisation, experimentation, forms, APIs, CRM-connected journeys, analytics integrations and data-driven digital experiences. Ensure production features meet requirements for performance, Core Web Vitals, security, WCAG 2.2 accessibility, SEO and AI-search discoverability. Follow agreed engineering standards for code review, unit testing, Git workflows, CI/CD, deployment, release management, architecture review and change control. Work collaboratively with the Technical Lead, CRO & UX Team, Product Designer, Frontend Developer and QA/Test Analyst to support releases, resolve defects and improve the Sitecore ecosystem, documentation and technical debt. Who you are You have at least five years’ full-stack development experience, including three or more years’ hands-on experience with Sitecore XP or a similar enterprise digital experience platform. You have strong proficiency in .NET/C#, JavaScript or TypeScript, React or Next.js, responsive HTML and CSS. You have experience developing reusable component libraries, templates, renderings, personalisation solutions and analytics integrations in Sitecore or a comparable DXP. You have experience, or demonstrable readiness, to work with Sitecore XM Cloud, SitecoreAI, headless technologies, JSS, Next.js, Content SDK, Experience Edge and GraphQL. You are familiar with Azure, Git, CI/CD pipelines, automated deployments, code review, unit testing and Agile delivery. Experience with APIs, CRM-connected journeys, VWO or similar experimentation tools would be advantageous. You understand web performance, Core Web Vitals, security, WCAG 2.2 accessibility and A/B testing principles. You are collaborative, detail-oriented and comfortable using AI-assisted development tools while applying sound engineering judgement. To read more about the role please click here . This is a permanent, full-time role to be based at our Surry Hills campus in Sydney.   Why join us?   Bold, modern and agile, we’re Australia’s fastest-growing university, going from 164 students in 2014 to 40,000+ alumni across 115+ countries and 2000+ staff today. In 2020, Australian Financial Review named us one of the country’s most innovative companies. As we continue to establish ourselves as a truly global university, we never lose sight of our student-centric approach. Supported by teams of passionate people, you’ll find endless opportunities for professional development and career progression.  We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer and committed to creating an inclusive workplace. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, colour, religion, age, ethnicity, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, or any other protected characteristic. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all positions.    What we offer:   We support your personal passions, development and wellbeing, to make your working life a more rewarding experience. At Torrens University Australia, you’ll benefit from:  Study free in a course/degree related to your position    B Corp certified university – values driven, and purpose led Access to internal opportunities - Be supported to learn, grow and move across the organisation    Hiring process   We aim to provide you with the information you need at each stage of this process to help you present your best self.  If you have any accessibility requirements, please contact your recruiter at Nikeey.silwal@torrens.edu.au for confidential support. We are committed to ensuring an equitable, barrier-free application process and have a Reasonable Adjustment Procedure in place to support you throughout the recruitment process.    To learn more about what makes Torrens University Australia a great place to work, visit https://www.torrens.edu.au/blog .    We’d love to hear from you. Job reference: R31591 Applications for this role will close on Monday 21st December. Please note, we may close applications earlier should a suitable candidate be identified. You can expect to hear from our Talent Acquisition team after this date with updates regarding your application.  Our office will be closed from 18th December and over the Christmas period, which may cause delays in processing your application. We kindly ask that you allow up to 3 additional weeks after the application closing date for any updates. If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Surry-Hills/Technical-Lead--Sitecore-_R31590": {
      "title": "Technical Lead (Sitecore)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-23\nFull time\n\nWho we are?   At Torrens University Australia, making a difference is in our DNA. As a Certified B Corporation, we belong to a global community of future-focused companies using business as a force for good. We believe in the transformative power of education to change lives, families, communities – and the world. That’s why we’re on a mission to increase access to higher education, so learners from all walks of life can chase their dreams.     Just like our students, our employees are a diverse group who want to make an impact. When you join us, we give you the freedom to be bold, creative, and courageous – with flexible working arrangements that allow you to bring your best. We’ve built a culture that celebrates community, collaboration, and innovation, where people love what they do .     What’s the job?   As Technical Lead (Sitecore), you will own the technical architecture, solution design, development standards and governance for Torrens University Australia’s in-house CRO & UX Team. Working within Architecture & Engineering and reporting to the Director - Architecture & Engineering, you will define the technical guardrails that enable the team to design, build, test and deploy conversion-focused digital experiences at speed, while maintaining IT governance, platform integrity and agreed engineering standards. You will act as the primary technical interface between the CRO & UX Team and IT, managing the balance between fast-lane delivery such as A/B testing, landing pages and UX improvements, and slow-lane work such as platform changes, security-impacting work and complex integrations. This is a high-autonomy leadership opportunity for an experienced digital platform technologist who can lead delivery across established and modern headless, personalisation and AI-driven platforms.  Principal accountabilities include (but are not limited to): Own the technical architecture, coding standards, development guardrails and governance for CRO-delivered work across the university’s digital experience platforms, currently Sitecore XP. Define and maintain standards for component development, personalisation, tracking, performance, security, accessibility, code review, testing, deployment and release management. Lead the technical approach for experimentation and personalisation, including the coexistence and future convergence of VWO, rules-based personalisation, Sitecore Personalize and CDP. Act as the primary technical interface with IT, ensuring appropriate engagement for platform risks, infrastructure issues, security matters, complex integrations and changes requiring Architecture Review Board approval. Lead and mentor the Sitecore Developer, QA/Test Analyst and Frontend Developer, while supporting technical feasibility, estimation, planning, productionisation of winning experiments and delivery sequencing. Own CRO code repositories, technical decision-making, weekly planning, code check-in reporting and monthly technical reviews, while contributing to DevOps, CI/CD, SitecoreAI adoption, documentation and technical debt reduction. Who you are You have at least eight years’ software engineering experience, including four or more years in technical leadership or lead developer roles. You have deep expertise in Sitecore XP or a similar enterprise digital experience platform, including architecture, MVC/SXA component development, templates, rendering strategies, rules-based personalisation and xDB/xConnect. You have strong full-stack proficiency across .NET/C#, JavaScript/TypeScript and modern front-end technologies such as React or Next.js. You have experience with Sitecore XM Cloud, SitecoreAI or a comparable headless/composable DXP, including JSS, Next.js or Content SDK, Experience Edge, GraphQL, the Pages editor and Sitecore Personalize/CDP. You have experience defining engineering standards, governance frameworks and deployment processes in an enterprise environment, with working knowledge of Azure, CI/CD, DevOps, change management and release management. You are an effective technical leader who can negotiate with central IT, mentor developers, review code, build team capability and balance delivery speed with platform integrity. Experience with CRO programs, experimentation tools such as VWO, web performance, security, WCAG 2.2 and AI-assisted development would be advantageous. To read more about the role please click here . This is a permanent, full-time role to be based at our Surry Hills campus in Sydney.   Why join us?   Bold, modern and agile, we’re Australia’s fastest-growing university, going from 164 students in 2014 to 40,000+ alumni across 115+ countries and 2000+ staff today. In 2020, Australian Financial Review named us one of the country’s most innovative companies. As we continue to establish ourselves as a truly global university, we never lose sight of our student-centric approach. Supported by teams of passionate people, you’ll find endless opportunities for professional development and career progression. We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer and committed to creating an inclusive workplace. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, colour, religion, age, ethnicity, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, or any other protected characteristic. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all positions.    What we offer:   We support your personal passions, development and wellbeing, to make your working life a more rewarding experience. At  Torrens University Australia, you’ll benefit from:     Study free in a course/degree related to your position     B Corp certified university – values driven, and purpose led Access to internal opportunities - Be supported to learn, grow and move across the organisation      Hiring process   We aim to provide you with the information you need at each stage of this process to help you present your best self. If you have any accessibility requirements, please contact your recruiter at Nikeey.silwal@torrens.edu.au for confidential support. We are committed to ensuring an equitable, barrier-free application process and have a Reasonable Adjustment Procedure in place to support you throughout the recruitment process.    To learn more about what makes Torrens University Australia a great place to work, visit https://www.torrens.edu.au/blog .    We’d love to hear from you. Job reference: R31590 Applications for this role will close on Monday 21st December. Please note, we may close applications earlier should a suitable candidate be identified. You can expect to hear from our Talent Acquisition team after this date with updates regarding your application.  Our office will be closed from 18th December and over the Christmas period, which may cause delays in processing your application. We kindly ask that you allow up to 3 additional weeks after the application closing date for any updates. If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Surry-Hills/Associate-Dean-Research---Innovation_R31513-1": {
      "title": "Associate Dean Research & Innovation",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-23\nFull time\n\nAssociate Dean Research & Innovation in the School of Technology   Who we are?   At Torrens University Australia, making a difference is in our DNA. As a Certified B Corporation, we belong to a global community of future-focused companies using business as a force for good. We believe in the transformative power of education to change lives, families, communities – and the world. That’s why we’re on a mission to increase access to higher education, so learners from all walks of life can chase their dreams.     Just like our students, our employees are a diverse group who want to make an impact. When you join us, we give you the freedom to be bold, creative, and courageous – with flexible working arrangements that allow you to bring your best. We’ve built a culture that celebrates community, collaboration, and innovation, where people love what they do . The Opportunity   This is a new role responsible for providing strategic and operational leadership across research, innovation, research training, industry-partnered research and external engagement. Working closely with the Dean of Technology School and the Deputy Vice-Chancellor Research & Innovation, you will help shape a high-quality, applied, industry-engaged and impact-focused research culture. The role will contribute to the University’s ambition to be a university for the real world by strengthening research capability, improving research performance, growing external partnerships and ensuring research creates meaningful value for students, industry, communities and the wider profession.    Principle accountabilities: Lead the development and implementation of the School’s Research & Innovation Plan, aligned with University strategy and priorities. Support the School to achieve research performance targets, including quality outputs, research income, HDR completions, external engagement and measurable impact. Build research capability by supporting academic staff with research planning, grant applications, publications, applied research and collaborative research profiles. Support the effective development of Higher Degree by Research activity, including recruitment, supervision quality, progress, completion outcomes and student experience. Promote research quality, integrity, ethics, governance, compliance and evidence-informed performance improvement. Develop industry, government, community, professional body and international partnerships that create opportunities for applied research, innovation and impact. Identify opportunities for interdisciplinary and cross-School collaboration, particularly where research connects with curriculum, employability, work-integrated learning and industry engagement. Represent the School in University-wide research strategy, governance, policy and performance initiatives. This role has the following workload allocation: Research leadership (40%): time dedicated to leading research activity within the role. Teaching (40%): time allocated to teaching responsibilities.  Personal research (20%): time allocated to the role-holder's own research program. Who you are: You will be an accomplished academic leader with a strong record in tertiary education, research and/or HDR leadership. You will bring the credibility, collaboration and strategic judgement needed to engage research-active staff, build partnerships and translate priorities into measurable outcomes. A postgraduate or doctoral qualification, preferably relevant to the School, or equivalent relevant industry experience. A significant track record of leadership in tertiary education, research and/or HDR programs, including contribution to policy, processes and governance. Demonstrated contribution to knowledge and research, including the beneficial application of knowledge and/or innovation in practice. Experience leading innovation, developing external relationships and building collaborative research or industry partnerships. Experience developing and leading high-performing teams, with a commitment to positive leadership, inclusion and staff development. Strong communication, relationship-building, analytical and influencing skills, with the ability to work across schools, disciplines and professional teams. To read more about the role please click here . This is a permanent, full-time position that can be based at any of our campus locations: Sydney, Melbourne, Adelaide or Brisbane.  Why join us?   Bold, modern and agile, we’re Australia’s fastest-growing university, going from 164 students in 2014 to 40,000+ alumni across 115+ countries and 2000+ staff today. In 2020, Australian Financial Review named us one of the country’s most innovative companies. As we continue to establish ourselves as a truly global university, we never lose sight of our student-centric approach. Supported by teams of passionate people, you’ll find endless opportunities for professional development and career progression.  We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer and committed to creating an inclusive workplace. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, colour, religion, age, ethnicity, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, or any other protected characteristic.  We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all positions.  What you’ll gain from the role Shape the research and innovation agenda for the School of Technology. Strengthen research capability, partnerships and real-world impact across the University. Work with senior academic and professional leaders in a collaborative, future-focused environment. Contribute to Torrens University Australia’s mission to deliver research and education with meaningful impact. Hiring process   To express your interest, please submit a current CV and a brief statement (maximum two pages) outlining your suitability for the role, your relevant research and leadership experience, and your vision for research and innovation in the School of Technology. If you have any accessibility requirements, please contact your recruiter at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au for confidential support. We are committed to ensuring an equitable, barrier-free application process and have a Reasonable Adjustment Procedure in place to support you throughout the recruitment process.    To learn more about what makes Torrens University Australia a great place to work, visit https://www.torrens.edu.au/blog Applications close: Monday,21st December    Job reference: R31513 Please note that our office will be closed from 18th December and over the Christmas period, which may cause delays in processing your application. We kindly ask that you allow up to 3 additional weeks after the application closing date for any updates. If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    }
  },
